/-!
# Q_β Stage C — the σ₃-lift obligation + the Casoratian W₃ decision rule (machine-checked)

Bean `1jrh` closed with the c₃^even measurement
(`docs/audits/2026-07-02-1jrh-c3even-exact-measurement.md`) and the instrumented
H₄ Markov base (`docs/audits/2026-07-02-1jrh-h4-stagec-markov-infra.md`); the
**sole remaining open Stage-C item** is the categorical σ₃-lift
`Λ ∈ H₄(q)` of the decay operator (scope:
`docs/scope/2026-06-18-qbeta-c4-h4-tower-stage-c-scope.md` §2).  Mirroring the
s013 pattern (`QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget`), this file makes the
obligation and its downstream decision rule machine-checked **without
enumerating any Λ candidate** (the scope's no-fit rule):

1. **The obligation class** `StageCSigma3Lift` — the OPEN carrier (NO instance,
   §3b-tax honest-open-state).  Encoded fields: the C12 stabilization-constant-1
   reading of the level-4 rung (`c4even = tr_M^{H₄}(Λ) − tr_M^{H₃}(shadow)`,
   Stage-C infra audit §Finding), the σ₃-gating non-degeneracy (a σ₃-free lift
   has zero level-4 content — preflight §1.3 — so a valid lift must have
   `c4even ≠ 0`), and bar-evenness of both traces under the bar-involution `σ`.
   The scope's remaining two side-conditions — *derived from the decay
   categorical content* and *anchor-stability < 1%* — are archimedean /
   meta-level selection rules on candidate constructions; they are deliberately
   NOT class fields (the first is a provenance rule about how Λ may be produced,
   the second needs two substrate evaluations), and stay governed by the scope
   doc.  Nothing here asserts Λ exists.
2. **The rung Casoratian** `rungCasoratian` — the 2×2 determinant
   `W_k = c_k^even·c_{k+1}^odd − c_{k+1}^even·c_k^odd` of adjacent ladder rungs
   (distinct from the q-difference-equation Casoratian of
   `QOU.QBeta.casoratian_abel`, which concerns solution *functions*; this one is
   the sign test on the measured rung matrix).
3. **Sign-tier robustness** (`W2_pos_of_sign_tiers`): `W₂ > 0` for ANY rung
   values in the measured sign tiers (`c₂^even < 0`, `c₃^even > 0`,
   `c₂^odd = −1` proved, `c₃^odd < 0`) — the audit computed `W₂ ≈ +102.67` from
   the specific rungs; this theorem shows the positivity needs only the tiers,
   so `W₂ > 0` is robust to rung refinement within tier.
4. **The decision rule** (`one_recurrence_incompatible`,
   `sigma3_lift_kill_test`): a single Askey–Wilson / orthogonal-polynomial
   three-term recurrence carrying both parity channels forces constant
   Casoratian sign (`0 < W₂·W₃`); with `W₂ > 0` from the tiers, any valid lift
   whose genuine rungs give `W₃ ≤ 0` refutes the one-recurrence identification
   — the machine-checked form of the 1jrh gated test.  (Scope-(a): it refutes
   *this identification*, not the ingredient.)

Base ring: generic `[CommRing R]` for the carrier and the Casoratian algebra;
the sign section adds `[LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R]` (ordering is
genuinely required for a sign test — §7c).  Sorry-free; no fit; no Λ candidate.

-- Ref: [gasper-rahman-2004] Basic Hypergeometric Series, 2nd ed., CUP 2004
--      (three-term recurrences and Casoratian positivity for orthogonal
--      polynomial systems, §7.7 Askey–Wilson).
-- Ref: [wenzl1988] https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01404457 (Markov trace weights).
-/

namespace QOU.QBeta.StageC

/-! ## The rung Casoratian (generic `CommRing`) -/

section Casoratian
variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The **rung Casoratian** `W = cₖᵉ·cₖ₊₁ᵒ − cₖ₊₁ᵉ·cₖᵒ` of two adjacent
ladder rungs, each carrying a bar-even and a bar-odd component.  For a ladder
generated by ONE three-term recurrence with bar-even multiplier
(`recurrence_invol_descent`), adjacent-rung Casoratians keep a constant sign;
`W` is the quantity the 1jrh sign test evaluates. -/
def rungCasoratian (cke ck1e cko ck1o : R) : R :=
  cke * ck1o - ck1e * cko

/-- With the **proved** rung `c₂^odd = −1` (Taylor-exact) substituted, the
`W₂` Casoratian collapses to `c₂^even·c₃^odd + c₃^even`. -/
theorem rungCasoratian_with_proved_c2odd (c2e c3e c3o : R) :
    rungCasoratian c2e c3e (-1) c3o = c2e * c3o + c3e := by
  simp only [rungCasoratian]
  ring

end Casoratian

/-! ## The obligation class (OPEN — Stage C §2; no instance) -/

/-- **Conjecture carrier (OPEN — the Stage-C σ₃-lift obligation; bean `1jrh`
handoff): the categorical lift `Λ ∈ H₄(q)` of the free-neutron-decay operator.**

A lift supplies its two Markov-trace values and the level-4 rung they induce:

* `trH4` — `tr_M^{H₄}(Λ)`, evaluable by the shipped Stage-C instrumented base
  (`computations/habiro/qbeta_h4_stagec_markov_infra.py`) once Λ is specified.
* `shadowH3` — `tr_M^{H₃}` of Λ's σ₃-free H₃ shadow.
* `c4even_eq` — the level-4 rung reads **directly** as the difference: the
  H₃→H₄ stabilization constant is exactly 1 in the Wenzl normalization
  (Stage-C infra audit, gate C12 at 1e-50 across 5 q-points), so no
  normalization constant intervenes.
* `sigma3_gating` — non-degeneracy: a σ₃-free element's H₄ data is fully
  determined by its H₃ data (branching preflight), hence carries zero level-4
  content; a valid lift must have `c4even ≠ 0`.
* `bar_even` / `shadow_bar_even` — both traces are fixed by the bar-involution
  `σ` (the scope's bar-evenness invariant; the ladder's even channel).

NO instance is provided: the open state is the honest state (§3b-tax).  The
scope's provenance rule (Λ must be *derived* from the decay categorical
content, never back-solved from a c₄ target) and the anchor-stability
side-condition are meta-level selection rules on constructions, not fields of
this carrier — see the module docstring. -/
class StageCSigma3Lift (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (σ : R →+* R) where
  /-- `tr_M^{H₄}(Λ)`. -/
  trH4 : R
  /-- `tr_M^{H₃}` of the σ₃-free H₃ shadow of Λ. -/
  shadowH3 : R
  /-- The induced level-4 (c₄^even) rung. -/
  c4even : R
  /-- C12 stabilization-constant-1 reading: `c₄^even = tr_M^{H₄}(Λ) − tr_M^{H₃}(shadow)`. -/
  c4even_eq : c4even = trH4 - shadowH3
  /-- σ₃-gating non-degeneracy: the lift carries genuine level-4 content. -/
  sigma3_gating : c4even ≠ 0
  /-- Bar-evenness of the H₄ trace. -/
  bar_even : σ trH4 = trH4
  /-- Bar-evenness of the H₃ shadow trace. -/
  shadow_bar_even : σ shadowH3 = shadowH3

/-- Any valid lift's rung is itself bar-even — derived from the two trace
fields via the C12 reading (the class composes; the rung inherits the ladder's
even-channel parity, as the scope's bar-evenness invariant demands). -/
theorem StageCSigma3Lift.c4even_bar_even {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (σ : R →+* R)
    [L : StageCSigma3Lift R σ] : σ L.c4even = L.c4even := by
  rw [L.c4even_eq, map_sub, L.bar_even, L.shadow_bar_even]

/-! ## The decision rule (ordered section — sign test) -/

section Decision
variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R]

/-- **Sign-tier robustness of `W₂ > 0`.**  For ANY rung values in the measured
sign tiers — `c₂^even < 0` (measured `≈ −8.006`), `c₃^even > 0` (measured
`≈ +86.66`), `c₂^odd = −1` (proved, Taylor-exact), `c₃^odd < 0` (near-match
`≈ −2`) — the `W₂` Casoratian is positive.  The audit's `W₂ ≈ +102.67` is an
instance; this shows the sign needs only the tiers. -/
theorem W2_pos_of_sign_tiers {c2e c3e c2o c3o : R}
    (h2e : c2e < 0) (h3e : 0 < c3e) (h2o : c2o = -1) (h3o : c3o < 0) :
    0 < rungCasoratian c2e c3e c2o c3o := by
  have hprod : 0 < c2e * c3o := mul_pos_of_neg_of_neg h2e h3o
  have hW : rungCasoratian c2e c3e c2o c3o = c2e * c3o + c3e := by
    rw [h2o]; exact rungCasoratian_with_proved_c2odd c2e c3e c3o
  rw [hW]
  linarith

/-- The Casoratian sign compatibility a SINGLE Askey–Wilson (orthogonal-
polynomial) three-term recurrence imposes on adjacent rung Casoratians:
constant sign, i.e. `0 < W₂·W₃`. -/
def casoratianSignCompatible (W2 W3 : R) : Prop := 0 < W2 * W3

/-- **The decision rule.**  With `W₂ > 0`, genuine c₄ rungs giving `W₃ ≤ 0`
are incompatible with the one-recurrence hypothesis.  Scope-(a): this refutes
the *single-AW-recurrence identification* of the ladder, not any ingredient. -/
theorem one_recurrence_incompatible {W2 W3 : R} (hW2 : 0 < W2) (hW3 : W3 ≤ 0) :
    ¬ casoratianSignCompatible W2 W3 := by
  intro h
  exact absurd h (not_lt.mpr (mul_nonpos_of_nonneg_of_nonpos hW2.le hW3))

/-- **The Stage-C kill-test, composed (machine-checked form of the 1jrh gated
test).**  Any valid σ₃-lift feeds the decision: under the measured sign tiers
(`W₂ > 0` by `W2_pos_of_sign_tiers`), if the lift's genuine `c₄^even` rung and
a genuine (beyond-CAL-anchor) `c₄^odd` rung give `W₃ ≤ 0`, the single-AW-
recurrence identification is refuted.  The indicative `W₃ < 0` lean from the
untrusted c₄ inputs (c₃^even measurement audit) is exactly the scenario this
theorem would convert into a decision once genuine rungs exist. -/
theorem sigma3_lift_kill_test (σ : R →+* R) [L : StageCSigma3Lift R σ]
    {c2e c3e c2o c3o c4odd : R}
    (h2e : c2e < 0) (h3e : 0 < c3e) (h2o : c2o = -1) (h3o : c3o < 0)
    (hW3 : rungCasoratian c3e L.c4even c3o c4odd ≤ 0) :
    ¬ casoratianSignCompatible (rungCasoratian c2e c3e c2o c3o)
        (rungCasoratian c3e L.c4even c3o c4odd) :=
  one_recurrence_incompatible (W2_pos_of_sign_tiers h2e h3e h2o h3o) hW3

end Decision

end QOU.QBeta.StageC
